{"resourceIdentifier":"3602","resourceName":"Udzungwa Corridor Reforestation","description":"Udzungwa Corridor Limited will reforest 7500 ha of bracken fern thicket on the Eastern Slopes of the Udzungwa Mountains in Tanzania by planting over 100 native tree species.\r\n\r\nThe project area is largely fallow farmland on steep slopes with no road access. Natural regeneration in the project area is prevented by a dense thicket of bracken fern, occasional cultivation, and hot fires when the bracken burns. The project is signing 30-year leases with the small holder farmers and village councils that own the project lands. The project covers all the costs associated with tree nursery establishment and tree planting and employs hundreds of local community members in the process. To ensure that the planted trees survive, the project is weeding around the planted seedlings 3 times a year for 3 years, clearing fire breaks around the planted areas, and employing firefighting teams.\r\n\r\nThe project is a 30-year project and will remove approximately 5,322,834 tCO2e over the project lifetime.\r\n\r\nThe project will greatly improve the local economy in the participating villages through reliable payments for leased land, creating hundreds of well-paying jobs, the provision of avocado seedlings and improved bean seed outside the planting area and funding village development projects. With 30 years of funding already secured by the project, the economic opportunities created by the project will be much more reliable than farming and thus help communities adapt to uncertain climate conditions. \r\n\r\nThe project is located in the Eastern Arc Biodiversity hotspot and will create a forest corridor that will reconnect the Udzungwa Scarp and Kilombero Nature Reserves. The corridor will increase habitat connectivity for the endangered Sanje Mangabey, vulnerable Udzungwa Red Colobus Monkey, and several other endangered and vulnerable species. Additionally, the project is planting vulnerable tree species, thereby directly increasing the population of vulnerable species in the area.","location":{"latitude":-8.214090,"longitude":36.089930},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-08-22","endExclusive":"2022-09-22","endInclusive":"2022-09-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3602"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Iringa and Morogoro Regions"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Udzungwa Corridor Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"Iringa, Tanzania"},{"type":"string","value":"+255765980601"},{"type":"string","value":"admin@udzungwacorridor.co.tz"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"178047"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"7500 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AENOR CONFIA, S.A. (UNIPERSONAL)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"20/11/2023"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 03/02/2022 - 02/02/2052"}]}]},{"programCode":"CCB","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Udzungwa Corridor Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"Iringa, Tanzania"},{"type":"string","value":"+255765980601"},{"type":"string","value":"admin@udzungwacorridor.co.tz"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Validation approved"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1780